# Code owners for spectrafit-core.
#
# TWO COPIES EXIST ON PURPOSE: this file (repo root) and .github/CODEOWNERS.
# GitLab (the primary remote / merge target, see CONTRIBUTING.md) only reads
# CODEOWNERS from the repo root, docs/, or .gitlab/ — it never looks under
# .github/, so a CODEOWNERS living only at .github/CODEOWNERS is inert on the
# source of truth and would only ever govern PRs on the disposable GitHub
# mirror. GitHub, conversely, only matches CODEOWNERS at the repo root,
# docs/, or .github/. Keeping one copy in each location is the only way for
# both hosts to honor it. Keep the two files' content in sync by hand; there
# is no generator for this today.
#
# GitHub matches this file only as `CODEOWNERS` (or `.github/CODEOWNERS`), and on
# a case-insensitive filesystem a lowercase `codeowners` is the SAME file locally
# while being invisible to GitHub. Keep the name uppercase.
#
# Single maintainer today; every other committer is a CI automation account. The
# per-area lines are not redundant with the catch-all — they are where a second
# maintainer gets added without having to reason about the whole tree.

*                       @Anselmoo

